<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2021/01/touch-bar-close-up.jpg" alt="" width="160" height="90" class="brief" align="left" style="float:left;margin:0 20px 20px 0;width:160px;height:auto;" />Apple introduced the Touch Bar 10 years ago today. At its <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2016/10/27/apple-unveils-touch-bar-macbook/">"Hello again" event</a> on October 27, 2016, Apple pitched the OLED Multi-Touch strip as "revolutionary." It replaced the MacBook Pro's function keys and divided users from the start, arriving in the same controversial redesign as the butterfly keyboard and removal of HDMI, SD card, and MagSafe ports.<br/>
<br/>
